--TEST--
`Core\Sse->retry` refuses a negative reconnection time rather than reading it as no wait at all — `rule:errors/ambiguous-input-refused`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// A client waits this long before it comes back, so a negative wait is not a
// shorter one — it is a sentence the wire cannot spell. Taking it as "no wait"
// would answer a question the program did not ask, which is the silent wrong
// answer a refusal exists instead of. A `LogicError` and not a diagnostic: the
// wait can be computed, so what was wrong is the value and not the call.
var $refused = "";
try {
    Core\Out::capture(fn (): void => {
        var $sse = Core\Sse::stream();
        $sse->retry(Core\Time\Duration::hours(1)->negated());
    });
} catch (LogicError $caught) {
    $refused = $caught->message;
}
echo $refused, "\n";

// The other side of the bound: no wait at all is a wait the wire can spell, so
// a zero-length one is written rather than refused.
var $none = Core\Out::capture(fn (): void => {
    var $sse = Core\Sse::stream();
    $sse->retry(Core\Time\Duration::seconds(0));
});
echo $none;
--EXPECT--
Core\Sse::retry(): a reconnection time cannot be negative: a client waits this long before it comes back, and there is no wait shorter than none
retry: 0

